  "strategy": "1.Approachandrationale  \n   We adopt a constructive heuristic based on periodic patterns and multi-scale optimization. Unlike the parent's random restart approach, we design h(x) by exploiting aperiodic overlapping and peak alignment. Rationale: The problem requires minimizing the maximum overlap between h(x) and its shifted versions. By decomposing h(x) into a sequence of distinct segments (blocks) with optimized peak positions and shapes, we can systematically reduce correlation across scales. This avoids local optima encountered by random search. We use gradient descent and adaptive block configuration to optimize the overall correlation.\n\n2.Mathematicalspecification  \n   We represent h(x) as:\n        h(x) = sum_{i=1}^M (scale_i \u00b7 indicator(B_i(x)))  \n   where B_i(x) are intervals, and scale_i \u2208 [0,1] with \u222bh(x)dx = 1/2.  \n   Objective:\n        C5 = max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx  \n   Subject to:\n        0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1\n        \u222b\u2080\u00b2h(x)dx = 0.5\n   We optimize over block configurations {B_i, scale_i} and k. The correlation is computed via asymptotic integration at relevant lags (k where h(x+k) overlaps significantly).\n\n3.Implementationprocedure  \n   Step1: Initialize with candidate sequences (several periods of sinusoidal waves and random intervals).  \n   Step2: For each period P, generate M = 280//P segments.  \n   Step3: Define each segment as a combination of two peaks separated by a configurable distance d.  \n   Step4: Use L-BFGS-B optimizer to minimize C5 over scaling factors s_j, while maintaining integral constraint.  \n   Step5: Adjust d and peak half-widths adaptively based on observed max correlation.  \n   Step6: Evaluate the final candidate with `objective` via finite-difference gradient computation.  \n\n4.Searchchoicesandvariations  \n   - Base structures: sin(x) + noise, sawtooth patterns  \n   - Autocorrelation penalty: min(k ||cross correlation at lag k|| for k in key lags)  \n   - Peak enrichment: adaptive insertion of multiple peaks per segment  \n   - Abandon early if improvement stalls  \n\n5.Computebudgetandrobustness  \n   - Dominant cost: ~20 optimization iterations * 280 evaluations = ~56000 (reasonable)  \n   - Timeout: if candidates exceed 85s, return best solution found  \n   - Fallback: use EM tree + isoperimetric optimization if no candidate improves upon parent  \n\n6.Validationandreturncontract  \n   - Feasibility: verify h(x) \u2208 [0,1] and \u222bh(x)dx=0.5\u00b11e-6  \n   - Minimization: new C5 < parent's 0.381375\u00b10.001  \n   - Format: (optimized_h, min_C5, 280)  \n   Modified objective uses mode='same' for circular shifts (better for local correlation detection).  \n   Implementation: use exponential weighting of correlation scores.",
